{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_019ts2pqY6gm7KCAkz28vRrd", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1\t\"\"\"Hold back the orders placed by blocked customers.\n2\t\n3\tA blocklist is a sequence of customer IDs, assembled from several\n4\tsources, so it can repeat an ID. Customer IDs are integers from 0 to\n5\t``2**24 - 1``.\n6\t\"\"\"\n7\t\n8\tfrom collections.abc import Sequence\n9\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n10\t\n11\t\n12\t@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\n13\tclass Order:\n14\t    \"\"\"One customer order.\n15\t\n16\t    Attributes\n17\t    ----------\n18\t    order_id : int\n19\t        Unique order number.\n20\t    customer_id : int\n21\t        ID of the customer who placed the order.\n22\t    amount_cents : int\n23\t        Order total, in cents.\n24\t    \"\"\"\n25\t\n26\t    order_id: int\n27\t    customer_id: int\n28\t    amount_cents: int\n29\t\n30\t\n31\tdef held_orders(\n32\t    orders: Sequence[Order], blocked_customers: Sequence[int]\n33\t) -> list[Order]:\n34\t    \"\"\"Select the orders whose customer is on the blocklist.\n35\t\n36\t    Parameters\n37\t    ----------\n38\t    orders : sequence of Order\n39\t        Orders to screen, in arrival order.\n40\t    blocked_customers : sequence of int\n41\t        Blocked customer IDs, possibly repeated.\n42\t\n43\t    Returns\n44\t    -------\n45\t    list of Order\n46\t        Every order placed by a blocked customer, in the order given.\n47\t\n48\t    Notes\n49\t    -----\n50\t    Runs in O(n m) time for n orders and m blocklist entries.\n51\t    \"\"\"\n52\t    return [\n53\t        order for order in orders if order.customer_id in blocked_customers\n54\t    ]\n55\t"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3b32f786-5bbc-49f8-bc64-91d10e2d4907", "uuid": "6a191d81-da8e-4643-a480-8bb31697c43e", "timestamp": "2026-10-19T08:03:44.999Z"}
